;; emit refused: kernel.main.main takes 2 parameters: a binary's main takes the World alone (a main with parameters before the World runs under the loader's --run only)
;; a `main` with a parameter before the World: the loader's `--run` reads it from the arguments,
;; and a binary's start has the World alone to call `main` on, so the generator refuses the
;; closure rather than write a call the C compiler rejects (read the arguments with `get_args`)
(type (List T) (Nil) (Cons T (List T)))
(type Bool (False) (True))
(type World (World Int))
(extern exit ((code Int) (w World)) World)
(fn main ((code Int) (w World)) World (exit code w))
